From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:01:43 +0200
Subject: media: sun6i-isp: Give the params node a .link_validate

The params node is a video output device feeding a sub-device sink pad,
so v4l2_subdev_link_validate() delegates validation of that link back to
it. It had no entity operations at all, so every pipeline start printed

  video device 'sun6i-isp-params' does not implement .link_validate(),
  driver bug!

and the check was skipped.

The node carries metadata with a fixed format and no geometry, so there
is nothing for it to disagree with the processor about and the operation
returns success -- but it has to exist for the core to stop complaining
and to stop silently skipping the link.

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c | 20 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
index 111111111111..222222222222 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/sun6i-isp/sun6i_isp_params.c
@@ -845,6 +845,24 @@ static const struct v4l2_file_operations sun6i_isp_params_fops = {
 	.poll		= vb2_fop_poll,
 };
 
+/* Media Entity */
+
+/*
+ * The params node is a video output device feeding a sub-device sink pad, so
+ * the pipeline asks it to validate its own link. It carries metadata with a
+ * fixed format and no geometry, so there is nothing to disagree about --
+ * but the operation has to exist, or v4l2_subdev_link_validate() calls the
+ * driver a bug and skips the check.
+ */
+static int sun6i_isp_params_link_validate(struct media_link *link)
+{
+	return 0;
+}
+
+static const struct media_entity_operations sun6i_isp_params_entity_ops = {
+	.link_validate	= sun6i_isp_params_link_validate,
+};
+
 /* Params */
 
 int sun6i_isp_params_setup(struct sun6i_isp_device *isp_dev)
@@ -869,6 +887,8 @@ int sun6i_isp_params_setup(struct sun6i_isp_device *isp_dev)
 
 	pad->flags = MEDIA_PAD_FL_SOURCE | MEDIA_PAD_FL_MUST_CONNECT;
 
+	video_dev->entity.ops = &sun6i_isp_params_entity_ops;
+
 	ret = media_entity_pads_init(&video_dev->entity, 1, pad);
 	if (ret)
 		goto error_mutex;
-- 
